WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.343 --> 00:00:02.864
- Ch-che-kwilio?

00:00:02.864 --> 00:00:04.210
- [Voiceover] Are you serious?

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:06.517
- Shut the (beep) up, Caitlin.

00:00:06.533 --> 00:00:08.216
(latin music)

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:11.932
- My disclaimer is that
there is like a gene

00:00:11.932 --> 00:00:14.115
in my family for being bad at languages.

00:00:14.115 --> 00:00:15.137
- I went to Spain this summer.

00:00:15.137 --> 00:00:16.298
- I took only French.

00:00:16.298 --> 00:00:18.573
- I'm hoping I don't
embarrass myself too much.

00:00:18.573 --> 00:00:20.013
- [Voiceover] Een-ya-ree-too.

00:00:20.013 --> 00:00:23.346
- Uh, I have absolutely no
clue how to pronounce this.

00:00:23.346 --> 00:00:25.529
- There's already, like, three hats

00:00:25.529 --> 00:00:27.410
on top of these letters that I don't know.

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:28.478
- In-ah-rih-too.

00:00:28.478 --> 00:00:31.254
- In-ah-roo-tee? In-ah-roo, In-a, Inn...

00:00:31.254 --> 00:00:33.019
- In-ya-ree-too.

00:00:33.019 --> 00:00:34.203
- Ooh, I didn't roll the "r" enough.

00:00:34.203 --> 00:00:35.271
Een-ya-rree-too.

00:00:35.271 --> 00:00:38.034
- 'Cause in America, you
can't say anything correctly.

00:00:38.034 --> 00:00:40.031
You just say it anyways.

00:00:40.031 --> 00:00:42.157
- [Voiceover] Peh-nya nyeh-toe.

00:00:42.157 --> 00:00:45.166
- Oh, don't make me butcher
the president's name.

00:00:45.166 --> 00:00:46.512
- So, like, I should probably know that.

00:00:46.512 --> 00:00:47.905
- It looks like it's penne.

00:00:47.905 --> 00:00:50.506
- Penne nay-oh-toe, penne nay-oh-toe.

00:00:50.506 --> 00:00:52.642
No (laughs), I just said the same thing.

00:00:52.642 --> 00:00:53.687
- Pee-nah?

00:00:53.687 --> 00:00:55.568
What the (beep) is "e" again?

00:00:55.568 --> 00:00:58.400
Is it like an "i" or an "a" or what is it?

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.341
- [Voiceover] Ah-yeer-ah-gah-rye.

00:01:00.341 --> 00:01:02.709
- There's so many letters in this word.

00:01:02.709 --> 00:01:04.102
- There's way too many "g's" and "r's".

00:01:04.102 --> 00:01:06.378
- Oh my god, this poor
kid in elementary school.

00:01:06.378 --> 00:01:07.817
Name was probably butchered all the time.

00:01:07.817 --> 00:01:09.744
- The first part of it
looks like Aguilera.

00:01:09.744 --> 00:01:13.426
- Ag (laughs) ag-yoo-ehrgh ehrgh (laughs).

00:01:13.426 --> 00:01:14.843
- Ag-ah-ree-gah-reh-reh.

00:01:14.843 --> 00:01:16.863
- Ah-goo-gah-ray?

00:01:16.863 --> 00:01:19.324
- Ah-geh-rah, gah-reh, ah-geh-rah-gah-reh?

00:01:19.324 --> 00:01:20.787
- Ah-gah-ree-gah-reh.

00:01:20.787 --> 00:01:22.575
- Irr-reh-gar-ay?

00:01:22.575 --> 00:01:23.527
- How do you say it?

00:01:23.527 --> 00:01:24.943
- [Voiceover] Vahl-dehr-rrah-mah.

00:01:24.943 --> 00:01:26.429
- I know this one, That 70's Show.

00:01:26.429 --> 00:01:27.869
- Vahl-der-ma-ma.

00:01:27.869 --> 00:01:28.983
- Vahl-dehr-rrah-mah.

00:01:28.983 --> 00:01:31.713
- Vahl-du-rhama, rh, rha-mah.

00:01:31.713 --> 00:01:33.594
- [Voiceover] Say-ah-choe-kay.

00:01:33.594 --> 00:01:36.125
- This looks like a shoe
brand or something like that.

00:01:36.125 --> 00:01:38.423
Sie-shi?

00:01:38.423 --> 00:01:39.783
- Shah-shoe? Oh man.

00:01:39.783 --> 00:01:40.991
See-ah-choo-koo?

00:01:40.991 --> 00:01:43.684
- Saw-she-koo? (laughs)
Wait no, no, no, no.

00:01:43.684 --> 00:01:44.636
- See-ah-coe-que?

00:01:44.636 --> 00:01:46.517
- See-ah-cho-kay?

00:01:46.517 --> 00:01:49.071
I just get images of somebody
being choked. (laughs)

00:01:49.071 --> 00:01:50.534
- [Voiceover] Ech-ay-ver-ee-ah.

00:01:50.534 --> 00:01:52.136
- [Voiceover] This is a sexier name.

00:01:52.136 --> 00:01:54.040
- I feel like this is a
really expensive water.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:55.665
Etch-ee-ah-very-ay?

00:01:55.665 --> 00:01:57.337
- Ech-i-veria.
- Ech-i-reh...(laughs)

00:01:57.337 --> 00:02:00.100
- I never judge people
who have thick accents.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.120
I'm always like, "Dude, I get it."

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:03.676
I just wanna say that for the record.

00:02:03.676 --> 00:02:05.765
- Hopefully I wouldn't offend
someone if I said their name.

00:02:05.765 --> 00:02:07.878
- [Voiceover] Zuluaga.

00:02:07.878 --> 00:02:09.225
- These are Spanish, really?

00:02:09.225 --> 00:02:10.595
- Zoo-laga?

00:02:10.595 --> 00:02:11.593
Oh, the Z's silent?

00:02:11.593 --> 00:02:13.497
- Zoo-lah, Zoo-lah-ga?

00:02:13.497 --> 00:02:15.494
- Zulu-lagah. (laughs)

00:02:15.494 --> 00:02:16.957
- Zulu-agah.

00:02:16.957 --> 00:02:19.000
I'm getting images of like Fabio but Latin

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.370
for some reason. (laughs)

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:21.926
- [Voiceover] Palazuelos.

00:02:21.926 --> 00:02:24.132
- Pah-lah-zulus?

00:02:24.132 --> 00:02:25.269
- Pah-lah-zay-loos?

00:02:25.269 --> 00:02:26.244
- Palazuelos.

00:02:26.244 --> 00:02:27.963
- Pah-lah-swe-los.

00:02:27.963 --> 00:02:30.540
Everyone's so excited, 'cause I proved

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:33.324
that I'm not a complete moron.

00:02:33.688 --> 00:02:35.290
- I felt like the substitute
teacher who, you know,

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:36.753
can't pronounce anybody's name.

00:02:36.753 --> 00:02:37.960
- It was a massacre.

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:39.075
There's, like, no excuse.

00:02:39.075 --> 00:02:40.537
- All of them are very sexy.

00:02:40.537 --> 00:02:41.884
- Latin America, I'm sorry.

00:02:41.884 --> 00:02:43.602
If it makes you feel
better, I'm not much better

00:02:43.602 --> 00:02:46.038
with English names.

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:49.036
(laughs) The audio
department's laughing at me.

00:02:49.036 --> 00:02:50.684
The director's laughing at me.

00:02:50.684 --> 00:02:51.683
Save your comments.

00:02:51.683 --> 00:02:54.683
I already got all the heat
when it actually happened.

